
  [1mThe fork:[0m [38;5;153mlogin(username, password)[39m runs [3mbefore[0m anyone is identified — the stub's own output is [38;5;153m{ success: true, user:
[39m  [38;5;153musername }[39m, so the identity is the result of logging in, not an input to it. The submit handler at [38;5;153mapp.js:19-20[39m only
  has the two form fields, so there is no [38;5;153muserId[39m available to pass. What "add a userId parameter" means depends on which
  of these you actually have:

  - [1mA caller-supplied id that already exists[0m (device id, tenant id, account number typed into the form) — then a third
    parameter is right, but the form needs a source for it, and I'd add an input to [38;5;153mindex.html[39m. Changes the public
    signature and the HTML; both cheap to revise now, annoying once the real API call replaces the stub.
  - [1mTracking the identity login produces[0m — then the parameter is the wrong shape; the right move is logging off the
    return value (or the API response once it's real), no signature change at all. Cheapest, and it can't go stale when
