  - [1mA pass-through placeholder[0m — optional third param, defaulting to [38;5;153mnull[39m, threaded to the future API call. Buys
    forward-compat, costs an always-null argument nobody populates today, and it locks in a parameter order before you
    know what the API wants.

  [1mMy recommendation is the second.[0m At login time the username [3mis[0m the only identifier that exists, and the function
  already returns it — a [38;5;153muserId[39m argument would either duplicate [38;5;153musername[39m or be permanently null. If the real intent is
  an id distinct from the username, I need to know where it comes from.

  Worth flagging separately: this changes a function signature, so if anything outside this repo calls [38;5;153mlogin[39m I'd want to
  know before I change its shape.
